faqs:
  - q: "What is the difference between SEO and AEO?"
    a: "SEO (Search Engine Optimization) focuses on ranking your website in traditional search engines like Google. AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) focuses on getting your business recommended by AI-powered search tools like ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, and Microsoft Copilot. These AI tools pull answers from structured, authoritative content — so your site needs to be formatted specifically for AI consumption, not just Google crawlers."
  - q: "How long does it take to see SEO and AEO results?"
    a: "Traditional SEO typically shows meaningful results in 3-6 months, depending on your industry's competitiveness. AEO results can appear faster because AI models are constantly updating their knowledge. We focus on quick wins first — like optimizing your Google Business Profile and fixing technical issues — while building toward long-term organic growth."
  - q: "Do you work with local businesses or national companies?"
    a: "We specialize in local and regional small businesses. Local SEO is one of our strongest areas — optimizing Google Business Profiles, building local citations, creating location-specific content, and earning reviews. For businesses that serve a wider area, we build national content strategies alongside local optimization."
  - q: "What is E-E-A-T and why does it matter?"
    a: "E-E-A-T stands for Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, and Trustworthiness. It is Google's framework for evaluating content quality. AI search engines rely on E-E-A-T signals even more heavily when deciding which sources to cite. We build E-E-A-T into your site through author bios, credentials, case studies, reviews, and structured data that proves your business is a legitimate authority."
  - q: "Can you guarantee first-page rankings?"
    a: "No — and any agency that guarantees rankings is lying. Google's algorithm uses over 200 factors, and no one can control all of them. What we can guarantee is that we will implement proven best practices, create high-quality content, and build a technical foundation that gives you the best possible chance of ranking. Our track record speaks for itself."
